{"findings":[{"file":"httpie/downloads.py","line":80,"what_goes_wrong":"A valid one-byte HTTP range is rejected because equal first and last byte positions are treated as invalid.","trigger":"Resuming at byte 0 when the server returns the complete one-byte resource header `Content-Range: bytes 0-0/1`.","expected":"The range denotes byte 0 and should return total size 1; this is also consistent with the adjacent comment, which only forbids a last position less than the first.","actual":"`parse_content_range` raises `ContentRangeError`.","confidence":"high","verified_by_running":true,"reproduction":"from httpie.downloads import parse_content_range\n\nassert parse_content_range('bytes 0-0/1', 0) == 1\n"},{"file":"httpie/sessions.py","line":127,"what_goes_wrong":"Reading `Session.cookies` removes each stored cookie's value, so a second read of the same session crashes.","trigger":"Assign a normal cookie jar containing `sid=v` to a `Session`, then access `session.cookies` twice.","expected":"A property that reconstructs the session's cookie jar should be repeatable and return the stored cookie each time.","actual":"The first access mutates the serialized cookie dictionary; the second raises `KeyError: 'value'`.","confidence":"high","verified_by_running":true,"reproduction":"from httpie.sessions import Session\nfrom requests.cookies import RequestsCookieJar, create_cookie\n\njar = RequestsCookieJar()\njar.set_cookie(create_cookie('sid', 'v'))\nsession = Session('unused.json')\nsession.cookies = jar\nsession.cookies\nsecond = session.cookies\nassert next(iter(second)).value == 'v'\n"},{"file":"httpie/sessions.py","line":140,"what_goes_wrong":"Saving cookies by name overwrites valid cookies that share a name but have different domains or paths.","trigger":"A session cookie jar contains `sid=first` for `a.example` and `sid=second` for `b.example`, such as after requests spanning domains through redirects.","expected":"Both cookies should survive session serialization, because cookie identity includes domain and path as well as name.","actual":"Only the final `sid` is retained and restored.","confidence":"high","verified_by_running":true,"reproduction":"from httpie.sessions import Session\nfrom requests.cookies import RequestsCookieJar, create_cookie\n\njar = RequestsCookieJar()\njar.set_cookie(create_cookie('sid', 'first', domain='a.example'))\njar.set_cookie(create_cookie('sid', 'second', domain='b.example'))\nsession = Session('unused.json')\nsession.cookies = jar\nrestored = session.cookies\nassert {(c.domain, c.name, c.value) for c in restored} == {\n    ('a.example', 'sid', 'first'),\n    ('b.example', 'sid', 'second'),\n}\n"},{"file":"httpie/plugins/manager.py","line":52,"what_goes_wrong":"Formatter plugins in the same group are silently discarded whenever that group appears in non-contiguous registration order.","trigger":"Register a default `format` formatter, a `colors` formatter, then another default `format` formatter; installed third-party formatters are appended after the built-ins, creating this order.","expected":"The `format` group should contain both formatters so all enabled processors run.","actual":"`groupby` creates two `format` runs and assignment to the dictionary overwrites the first, leaving only the last formatter.","confidence":"high","verified_by_running":true,"reproduction":"from httpie.plugins.base import FormatterPlugin\nfrom httpie.plugins.manager import PluginManager\n\nFirstFormat = type('FirstFormat', (FormatterPlugin,), {})\nColors = type('Colors', (FormatterPlugin,), {'group_name': 'colors'})\nSecondFormat = type('SecondFormat', (FormatterPlugin,), {})\nmanager = PluginManager()\nmanager.register(FirstFormat, Colors, SecondFormat)\nassert manager.get_formatters_grouped()['format'] == [FirstFormat, SecondFormat]\n"}],"what_examined":"Audited the request/input, client, download, session, output-processing, formatter, and plugin-manager paths; ran focused plain-Python reproductions for every reported finding. I also ran `pytest tests`; its remaining failures were documentation-tool or environment/platform related and were not reported as code defects."}
